title: 'Registrar: relayed para requests + deprecations'

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |-
      A para with no channel to the registrar parachain can now manage itself through the relay
      chain. It calls the new `pallet-registrar-relay::relay` with a `ParaRequest` (add or remove
      lock, deregister, schedule code upgrade, set current head), which is queued and forwarded as
      `MessageToParaV1::Relayed` in `on_poll`. `pallet-registrar-para` runs it as the new
      `Origin::RelayedPara` and reports the outcome in `RelayedRequest`.

      The queue is bounded by `MaxQueuedRequests` in total, `MaxQueuedPerPara` per para so one para
      cannot fill it, and `MaxForwardedPerBlock` per block. A request the transport refuses stays
      first in line.

      `pallet-registrar-relay::Config` now requires a `RuntimeOrigin` convertible into the
      parachains `Origin`, and `pallet-registrar-para::Config` one built from its own `Origin`.
      `pallet-registrar-relay`'s `WeightInfo` gains `relay`, `poll_relay_queue` and
      `forward_relayed`, `pallet-registrar-para`'s gains `receive_relayed`. `MessageToPara` no longer
      implements `MaxEncodedLen`. The `paras_registrar` calls get a `Deprecated` doc note.

crates:
  - name: registrar-primitives
    bump: major
  - name: pallet-registrar-para
    bump: major
  - name: pallet-registrar-relay
    bump: major
  - name: polkadot-runtime-common
    bump: none
